# Regression Test: Conditional parameterized exceptions preserve fallback

Tests that a conditional exception for a function-valued (`depends on`)
definition returns `none` when the condition is false, rather than returning
`some (fun ... => default)`.

The generated Lean4 exception leaf should have this shape:

```
if cond then some (fun (x : Int) => ...)
else none
```

It must not have this shape:

```
some (fun (x : Int) => match if cond then some (...) else none with
  | some r => r
  | _ => default)
```

```catala
declaration scope ConditionalParameterizedException:
  input cond content boolean
  output f content integer depends on x content integer
  output out content integer

scope ConditionalParameterizedException:
  label base_f
  definition f of x equals x + 1

  exception base_f
  definition f of x under condition cond consequence equals x + 100

  definition out equals f of 10
```
